WEBVTT

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.255
How do the four gears feed each other?

00:00:02.445 --> 00:00:05.856
Meet Nia, a fictional personal trainer in
Kigali.

00:00:05.996 --> 00:00:11.200
Follow one person from her first post to
the story that helps the next client find

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:11.525
her.

00:00:12.128 --> 00:00:14.457
Attract turns attention into interest.

00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:18.976
Nia posts about finding time to train
around a changing workweek.

00:00:19.116 --> 00:00:20.622
She offers a free planner.

00:00:20.762 --> 00:00:23.888
Dani signs up, giving Nia a way to follow
up.

00:00:24.503 --> 00:00:27.246
Engage turns interest into a conversation.

00:00:27.386 --> 00:00:31.526
Nia sends the planner and asks what usually
disrupts the week.

00:00:31.666 --> 00:00:33.894
Dani mentions late Tuesday meetings.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:38.098
That answer gives Nia something specific to
discuss on a fit call.

00:00:38.712 --> 00:00:42.288
Convert turns a qualified conversation into
paid work.

00:00:42.428 --> 00:00:45.953
On the call, Nia checks Dani’s goals and
availability.

00:00:46.093 --> 00:00:51.340
They agree on a four-week starter package
with a backup training time and weekly

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:51.715
check-ins.

00:00:52.337 --> 00:00:55.859
Ascend turns good delivery into future
opportunities.

00:00:55.999 --> 00:01:01.417
At their final review, Dani says choosing a
backup time made training easier to keep

00:01:01.417 --> 00:01:01.778
up.

00:01:01.918 --> 00:01:04.294
Nia asks permission to share that lesson.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:09.900
With permission, Nia puts that lesson in a
new post and links to the same planner.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:14.604
Another busy professional recognizes their
own problem and signs up.

00:01:14.744 --> 00:01:18.128
That is how Ascend feeds Attract and starts
the next loop.

00:01:18.753 --> 00:01:21.845
Look at where people stop moving forward in
your business.

00:01:21.985 --> 00:01:27.033
Take the free diagnostic below to find the
gear that needs attention first.

